text Gxcommit "{\n  \"sha\": \"e97222eb82f1ec56e852ba9571786db9ccc5c97a\",\n  \"node_id\": \"C_kwDOVQ5LydoAKGU5NzIyMmViODJmMWVjNTZlODUyYmE5NTcxNzg2ZGI5Y2NjNWM5N2E\",\n  \"commit\": {\n    \"author\": {\n      \"name\": \"Drake Stapleton\",\n      \"email\": \"drake@aienos.com\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-10-20T12:35:09Z\"\n    },\n    \"committer\": {\n      \"name\": \"Drake Stapleton\",\n      \"email\": \"drake@aienos.com\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-10-20T12:35:09Z\"\n    },\n    \"message\": \"P0: phase ledger with transferred issue numbers (#1 programme, #2..#9 = P0..P7)\",\n    \"tree\": {\n      \"sha\": \"2a83aef799f4c3c3585c2e29277cadc2f86c5b51\",\n      \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/aien-dev/allen/git/trees/2a83aef799f4c3c3585c2e29277cadc2f86c5b51\"\n    },\n    \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/aien-dev/allen/git/commits/e97222eb82f1ec56e852ba9571786db9ccc5c97a\",\n    \"comment_count\": 0,\n    \"verification\": {\n      \"verified\": false,\n      \"reason\": \"unsigned\",\n      \"signature\": null,\n      \"payload\": null,\n      \"verified_at\": null\n    }\n  },\n  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/aien-dev/allen/commits/e97222eb82f1ec56e852ba9571786db9ccc5c97a\",\n  \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/aien-dev/allen/commit/e97222eb82f1ec56e852ba9571786db9ccc5c97a\",\n  \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/aien-dev/allen/commits/e97222eb82f1ec56e852ba9571786db9ccc5c97a/comments\",\n  \"author\": {\n    \"login\": \"drakestapleton\",\n    \"id\": 213298340,\n    \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODLaspA\",\n    \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/213298340?v=4\",\n    \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n    \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/drakestapleton\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/drakestapleton\",\n    \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/drakestapleton/followers\",\n    \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/drakestapleton/following{/other_user}\",\n    \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/drakestapleton/gists{/gist_id}\",\n    \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/drakestapleton/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n    \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/drakestapleton/subscriptions\",\n    \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/drakestapleton/orgs\",\n    \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/drakestapleton/repos\",\n    \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/drakestapleton/events{/privacy}\",\n    \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/drakestapleton/received_events\",\n    \"type\": \"User\",\n    \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n    \"site_admin\": false\n  },\n  \"committer\": {\n    \"login\": \"drakestapleton\",\n    \"id\": 213298340,\n    \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODLaspA\",\n    \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/213298340?v=4\",\n    \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n    \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/drakestapleton\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/drakestapleton\",\n    \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/drakestapleton/followers\",\n    \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/drakestapleton/following{/other_user}\",\n    \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/drakestapleton/gists{/gist_id}\",\n    \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/drakestapleton/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n    \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/drakestapleton/subscriptions\",\n    \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/drakestapleton/orgs\",\n    \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/drakestapleton/repos\",\n    \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/drakestapleton/events{/privacy}\",\n    \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/drakestapleton/received_events\",\n    \"type\": \"User\",\n    \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n    \"site_admin\": false\n  },\n  \"parents\": [\n    {\n      \"sha\": \"2949450005a2df34e48da90bd40037841d49b3da\",\n      \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/aien-dev/allen/commits/2949450005a2df34e48da90bd40037841d49b3da\",\n      \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/aien-dev/allen/commit/2949450005a2df34e48da90bd40037841d49b3da\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"stats\": {\n    \"total\": 30,\n    \"additions\": 29,\n    \"deletions\": 1\n  },\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"sha\": \"d42f5dea4ca628f6ee539da8d2b732b52faf03ec\",\n      \"filename\": \"docs/PHASES.md\",\n      \"status\": \"modified\",\n      \"additions\": 29,\n      \"deletions\": 1,\n      \"changes\": 30,\n      \"blob_url\": \"https://github.com/aien-dev/allen/blob/e97222eb82f1ec56e852ba9571786db9ccc5c97a/docs%2FPHASES.md\",\n      \"raw_url\": \"https://github.com/aien-dev/allen/raw/e97222eb82f1ec56e852ba9571786db9ccc5c97a/docs%2FPHASES.md\",\n      \"contents_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/aien-dev/allen/contents/docs%2FPHASES.md?ref=e97222eb82f1ec56e852ba9571786db9ccc5c97a\",\n      \"patch\": \"@@ -1,3 +1,31 @@\\n # Phase ledger\\n \\n-Filled after the issue transfer (coordinator).\\n+Programme issue: [aien-dev/allen#1](https://github.com/aien-dev/allen/issues/1) (transferred 2026-10-20 from aien-architecture-mv#278; the old URL redirects, comments and history preserved).\\n+\\n+Phase numbers are sequence, not priority. Progress status words: PROPOSED, SCOPED, ACTIVE, IN_REVIEW, COMPLETE. Qualification verdicts are separate: PASS, FAIL, INCONCLUSIVE, NOT_RUN. A phase closes only with its acceptance evidence; the programme close guard (`guard/`) reopens the programme otherwise.\\n+\\n+| Phase | Issue here | Former issue | Title | Status | Qualification |\\n+|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n+| P0 | [#2](https://github.com/aien-dev/allen/issues/2) | arch#279 | Establish Allen's own repository, mission and B0 acceptance contract | ACTIVE (2026-10-20) | NOT_RUN |\\n+| P1 | [#3](https://github.com/aien-dev/allen/issues/3) | arch#280 | Build reproducible training episodes from the existing conversation archive | PROPOSED | NOT_RUN |\\n+| P2 | [#4](https://github.com/aien-dev/allen/issues/4) | arch#281 | Label human intent, corrections, successes and failures with evidence | PROPOSED | NOT_RUN |\\n+| P3 | [#5](https://github.com/aien-dev/allen/issues/5) | arch#282 | Freeze leakage-resistant evaluations and measure the baseline | PROPOSED | NOT_RUN |\\n+| P4 | [#6](https://github.com/aien-dev/allen/issues/6) | arch#283 | Train and compare a bounded first personal Allen candidate | PROPOSED | NOT_RUN |\\n+| P5 | [#7](https://github.com/aien-dev/allen/issues/7) | arch#284 | Qualify Allen B0 through one complete personal-assistance experience | PROPOSED | NOT_RUN |\\n+| P6 | [#8](https://github.com/aien-dev/allen/issues/8) | arch#285 | Keep one Allen continuous across iMac, Pi, Spark and MacBook | PROPOSED | NOT_RUN |\\n+| P7 | [#9](https://github.com/aien-dev/allen/issues/9) | arch#286 | Learn continually and anticipate useful help under bounded exploration | PROPOSED | NOT_RUN |\\n+\\n+Order: P0 -> P1 -> P2 -> P3 -> P4 -> P5 produces B0 only if its gates pass; P6 extends continuity to the four devices; P7 adds evaluated continual learning. P3's evaluation schema may be drafted during P1/P2, but evaluation data is isolated before any fitting, retrieval indexing or preference extraction.\\n+\\n+## Mandatory external prerequisites (programme cannot close while any is open)\\n+\\n+Verified OPEN when the gate was written (2026-10-20). The close guard reads this list from `guard/policy.toml`; keep both in step.\\n+\\n+| Area | Issues |\\n+|---|---|\\n+| Identity, persona, experience, release | aien-architecture-mv #159, #269, #190 |\\n+| Physical Pi to Spark execution and independent acceptance | aien-architecture-mv #231, #232; aienos-mv #396, #398, #399; aien-protocols-mv #27; aien-sovereign-core-mv #586; omega-mv #505; aegis-runtime-mv #53 |\\n+| Native Spark model path | aienos-mv #286, #327 (evaluated under aien-architecture-mv #190) |\\n+| Learning economics and out-of-sample evidence | aien-architecture-mv #246, #262, #263, #276; omega-mv #583, #584, #600 |\\n+\\n+P6 owns the remaining iMac and MacBook physical qualification if no existing issue owns it.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"
